  "rationale": "Solve by elimination: multiply x + 2y = 10 by 2 to get 2x + 4y = 20, then subtract 2x − y = 5 to get 5y = 15, so y = 3 (and back-substituting gives x = 4, matching the marked intersection (4, 3) on the graph). Choice C is the x-coordinate — the correct solution reported as the wrong component. Choice A comes from scaling only the variable terms of x + 2y = 10 (writing 2x + 4y = 10), which yields 5y = 5 and y = 1. Choice D comes from subtracting the left sides while adding the right sides, giving 5y = 25 and y = 5.",
